  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening achievements in maternal, newborn and child health in Koussan&#xe9;, Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">28 villages in Koussan&#xe9;, Mali (16.630 people reached)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community sensitization; capacity building/training of the health center staff and involved stakeholders; developing an exit plan with the involved stakeholder. This project is implemented at the same time as PRJ13-099-0004.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In previous projects, various activities have been implemented to increase the access to and quality of health care. A main achievement is the construction and operationalization of two new health centers. This project is aimed at responding to the final priority (health) needs and ensuring impact on the longer term. The ultimate aim is to improve the health of mothers and children and reduce the number of (preventable) death cases.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Koussan&#xe9;, Mali</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project to strengthen the achievements made in the previous MRC-NLRC projects on maternal, newborn and child health in Koussan&#xe9;, Mali.</narrative>
  </description>
